WEBVTT

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.960
Speaker 1: What if I told you that temptations are necessary?

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:27.220
Speaker 1: I mean, you cannot get to the next level of God's plan for your life without temptations.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.780
Speaker 1: This might be a perspective to overcoming temptations that you never saw coming.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:32.659
Speaker 1: All right?

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:38.820
Speaker 1: So if you stay to the end, this is going to really bless you, and it's going to change your perspective and how you respond to them.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.780
Speaker 1: This is day 26 of 100 days of discipleship.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.060
Speaker 1: What a time we've had.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.180
Speaker 1: I saw some of you crying on X about your test.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.820
Speaker 1: Sorry, sorry.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:48.580
Speaker 1: Don't cry.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.940
Speaker 1: You know, just pay attention.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:55.300
Speaker 1: Because like a thief in the night, we might just sip in the next one.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.940
Speaker 1: All right, Sipping the next one.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:08.100
Speaker 1: And let me also say this, doing well in the tests might contribute to you being invited here to the live sessions when they begin, okay?

00:01:08.579 --> 00:01:10.260
Speaker 1: That being said, let's move on.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.540
Speaker 1: Like I said, temptations are very necessary, very important aspects of growth.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.410
Speaker 1: You see, there are synonyms for temptation, tests, trials, all right?

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:34.170
Speaker 1: And even though some people try to change the context and the interpretation, as if all those words and terminologies strictly mean something different, as you would learn in this class, they are more alike, at least more alike than you realize.

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:40.650
Speaker 1: And you see, in education, if you see anyone in a class, it's because he passed tests.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.570
Speaker 1: You don't get promoted without passing tests.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:49.180
Speaker 1: There must be assessments, and that is what determines your promotion, all right?

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:54.620
Speaker 1: And that is one perspective that you must have to trials, tribulations and tests.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.100
Speaker 1: James, chapter one, from verse one.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:05.500
Speaker 1: From verse two, James says, count it all joy, my brothers, when you meet trials of various kinds.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.660
Speaker 1: He says, for you know that the testing of your faith produces steadfastness.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:14.220
Speaker 1: He says, there is something about tests that produce steadfastness.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:21.380
Speaker 1: You see, I'm a bit of a sports enthusiast, you know, Those of you who follow me know a bit about that.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:28.260
Speaker 1: And a lot of people have wondered why the Messi and Sir Ronaldo era lasted so long.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:45.090
Speaker 1: We've seen other greats in the past, but when you're talking about 15, 16, 17 years of shared dominance of every single Ballon d' or being shuffled between two people, of course, mostly messy, don't get me started, you know, but you get what I mean.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.250
Speaker 1: And people are wondering why they were able to endure so much.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:03:06.210
Speaker 1: But the reality is, at least people opine that because both of them were born in the same generation, there is a secret desire, you know, to outperform each other, or at least they both drive each other to better.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:10.930
Speaker 1: And this is how tests and Trials bring out the best in us.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.410
Speaker 1: And this is to the degree that James can say, count it all, joy.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.410
Speaker 1: Count it all, joy.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:23.010
Speaker 1: Just imagine someone hits tests so much he doesn't write exams.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.090
Speaker 1: In school, you're going to stay in the same class.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:33.070
Speaker 1: And I'm telling you that in the school of the Spirit there are some classes that you cannot enter without passing some tests.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:38.180
Speaker 1: In ordination, Paul says that you should not be hasty to lay hands.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:45.940
Speaker 1: And he says, do not ordain a novice lest he be lifted up with pride and fall to the smell of Satan.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:54.500
Speaker 1: Meaning there are some spiritual qualifications that are only for people who have gone through tests, who have been tested, who have scars.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:06.990
Speaker 1: There are some things that you have gone through in life, you know, and the moment you begin to talk, everybody who is going through the same will listen.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:14.750
Speaker 1: Because at least you understand, not everybody who preaches has experienced some things.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.870
Speaker 1: And make no mistake, experience is not the best teacher.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:21.950
Speaker 1: I don't have to experience everything to teach you the word of God.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.630
Speaker 1: But then it hits difference.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:30.840
Speaker 1: When someone who is going through something feels at the lowest ebb of his life like the world is going to end.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:36.920
Speaker 1: And then the person who is talking to you now says, well, guess what, I've been there.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.560
Speaker 1: You're going to be like what you know.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.360
Speaker 1: And that promotion is going to aid you in ministry more than you saw coming.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.840
Speaker 1: And the Bible says the testing of your faith produces steadfastness.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:56.470
Speaker 1: He says, let steadfastness have its full effect, that you may be perfect and complete and lacking in nothing.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:01.870
Speaker 1: There is something about trials and temptations that strengthen your muscles.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:03.270
Speaker 1: So this is what you need to realize.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.870
Speaker 1: You see that very habit that knocks you off all the time.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.030
Speaker 1: It's your ticket to the next level.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:28.330
Speaker 1: And when you sit with the word of God and with spirit driven determination and you cross to the other side, you just discover that there's a new layer of your work with God where Paul can say, it's a faithful saying worthy of all acceptance.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:35.930
Speaker 1: Meaning nobody can say this, God sent Christ to save sinners of whom I am chief.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.330
Speaker 1: My life has become a testimony.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:43.210
Speaker 1: If I made it out, you're going to make it out too, you know, so this is so important.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:55.140
Speaker 1: And then in verse 12 now someone says, well, are we not just lumping up trials and temptations to get us Here is something interesting.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:06:06.620
Speaker 1: So, well, James chapter one, verse three says, James chapter one, verse two talks about trials and then verse 12 talks about temptations, right?

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:14.660
Speaker 1: He said, blessed is the man who is steadfast on the trial, when he has stood the test, he shall receive the crown of life which God has promised to them that love him.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.620
Speaker 1: Let no man say when he's tempted.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.060
Speaker 1: And being tempted by God.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:26.059
Speaker 1: So now you are tempted to say, well, now there's a tendency for you to say, okay, trial is different.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:27.180
Speaker 1: Temptation is different.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:28.780
Speaker 1: Here is something shocking.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.980
Speaker 1: It's the same Greek word, pyrasmus.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:33.580
Speaker 1: Pyrasmus.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:39.510
Speaker 1: So in the Greek, Paul was James, I beg your pardon, was literally talking about the same thing.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:44.230
Speaker 1: And, well, there might be slight differences.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.790
Speaker 1: What makes one a trial and what makes one a temptation.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:53.630
Speaker 1: But I'm letting you know that temptations can be weaponized to bring out the best in you.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:54.550
Speaker 1: And this is the balance.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:57.670
Speaker 1: Because they bring out the best in you doesn't mean they are of God.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:01.150
Speaker 1: Let no one say when he's tempted by God.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:05.180
Speaker 1: God cannot be tempted with evil, and he doesn't tempt anyone.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.620
Speaker 1: So what God does, is that what the enemy meant for evil?

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.260
Speaker 1: He turns it around for good.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.780
Speaker 1: And that's why it says, count it.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.580
Speaker 1: All joy.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.380
Speaker 1: It's not a joyful experience, but it says, count it.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:20.619
Speaker 1: This is important.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.100
Speaker 1: So just.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.700
Speaker 1: Just think about it.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:28.140
Speaker 1: That temptation you're struggling with might be your ticket to the next level.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:36.160
Speaker 1: There are things that God can trust you with that becomes incumbent, that you overcome that temptation.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.040
Speaker 1: You enter into a new level.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.560
Speaker 1: God can trust you with more.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:47.960
Speaker 1: The Bible literally says that Jesus was led by the spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:59.890
Speaker 1: Sometimes the Lord allows it for your strength, for announcement in the realm of the spirit, for your muscles to be toughened.

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:03.690
Speaker 1: And the Bible says, having passed all the tests, Jesus returned.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:08.850
Speaker 1: In the power of the spirit, there is a power in overcoming trials.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:09.890
Speaker 1: This is your ticket.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:11.810
Speaker 1: This is your ticket.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:12.810
Speaker 1: Blessed is the man.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.130
Speaker 1: James 1:12.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:23.170
Speaker 1: Blessed is the man who remains steadfast under trial, for when he has stood the test, he shall receive the crown of life which God has promised to them that love him.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:30.360
Speaker 1: So trials really, actually attract, you know, rewards, supernatural rewards.

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.760
Speaker 1: And so the same prayer Jesus prayed for.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.440
Speaker 1: Peter, I pray for you.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:42.480
Speaker 1: Jesus said, simon, son of Barger, the enemy seeks to have you, that he may sift you like wheat.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.240
Speaker 1: He says, but I prayed for you that your faith should not fail.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:51.640
Speaker 1: It says, and when you are converted, strengthen your brother.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:52.760
Speaker 1: You see what I'm saying?

00:08:53.640 --> 00:09:00.120
Speaker 1: That when you pass through tests, it now equips you to be able to help others in the same.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.720
Speaker 1: In such a way that there is a message in your mess.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:07.720
Speaker 1: And that test will soon be a testimony.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:09.960
Speaker 1: If you believe that, say loud.
